I had just lost a tourist (post-quest) to an eel, so wanted
to take a break from tourists for a while.  Instead I did
archeologist - this is my first 'A' ascention

Begining was kinda normal.  I did a lot more tinning than
usual.  It really helps get intrinsics, because otherwise
you're satiated all the time, not to mention getting
poison resistance more easily. I don't have any notes from
the  early game, but I did minetown first, and got a few
points of protection from a vault and a bones file (he
left $2000 thankyouverymuch).

Found GoP (in a shop I think), coMR (from the bones file),
and a (blessed magic lamp somewhere in the mines).  Wielded
a mattock for a while, then two-weaponed a pick-axe
(eventually foo-proofed and +7 and named "Pathfinder") and
a silver saber.  Sokoban yielded reflection, so I went for
the castle - to wish for an artifact.  I wanted something to
give me MR that wouldn't take up a slot so I could wear a
robe.

Somewhere along the way I found a magic whistle and a
polytrap so I had matching red and black dragons in the
castle.  Did the Valley to get to XL14, Wished for a HoB,
Magic Mirror of Merlin.  I realize that getting the MMoM
isn't very useful, but else can a Lawful Archeologist get?
At least it's lighter the the Orb.  In fact, I don't think
I carried the orb around until the ascention run.

The quest was pretty easy, though I remember being confused
while.

I lost my ring of TC to a nymph (along with my AOLS) so I
tried polypilling for another.  Didn't get a ring, but did
manage to get 24(!!) scrolls of genocide.  Wondered for a
while what to do with them, and eventually decided to
genocide as much as possible just to see what happens.

Ultimatly genocided:  h,R,;,L,P,t,w,V,Z,M,n,Y,T,S,N,D,q,o,
g,d,f,b,a,O,H,r

Or a total of 157 species.  :-)

I also tried to get Grayswandir, and did some pudding
farming to convince Quatx to give it to me.  On the way, I
finished Gehenom with my pick-axe+silver-saber.  (wonderful
combo for digging and killing).

Finally got Grayswandir.  Did some foo-dancing, got my
level up to 30 (just so I wouldn't worry about eating wraith
corpses).  Did alchemy and got 66 !oFH.  I actually had to
drink all of them in the end- otherwise I would be burdend.
Decided to splurge with my remaining wishes and play with
a fully kitted Archon named Archibald.

Stormed the sanctum.  Found the wizard fighting the high
priest (but then they both turned on me).  Archibald was
killing things so fast, they didn't have time to use their
starting potions.  Found another 5 potions of Gain Level
in the sanctum graveyard(!).

Ascention run.  The mysterious force was really bad.

For the Astral plane I had another (regular) archon and my
guardian angel.  Found the correct altar on the first try,
but decided to have some fun.  My three 'A's tag-creamed
everyone.  I had to heal the angel and the second archon,
on occasion but Archibald never lost a hitpoint.  I don't
think I ever touched any of the riders...

